{"version":1,"content":"<html>\n<body>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DVS00773-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DVS00814-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DVS00845-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/JPEG影像-4714-8D56-4F-0-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC06619-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<p>兩間獨立書店「留下書舍」及「田園書屋」前日（15日）被國安警察上門拘捕。據了解，留下書舍有三人、田園書屋有兩人被捕，涉嫌違反《基本法》23條煽動罪。</p>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DSC06465-1024x683.jpeg\"/>\n<p>政府新聞稿指，警方國安處根據海關轉介，經調查後於旺角兩書店拘捕五人，並檢獲一批書籍，他們涉嫌違反《維護國家安全條例》第24條「具煽動意圖」罪。</p>\n<img src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Payme-500x237.png\"/>\n</body>\n</html>","scraped_at":"2026-07-17T13:59:58.221591+00:00","quality":{"score":1,"chars":159,"images":7,"source":"The Collective HK","fallback":"none"}}